{"name":"Red Bay","hex":"#8e3738","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Red Bay","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in Labrador, Newfoundland and Labrador.","A townland and bay in County Antrim, Northern Ireland."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Red_Bay"}],"entries":[{"title":"Red Bay, Alabama","blocks":[{"text":"Red Bay is a city in Franklin County, Alabama, United States. It was founded in 1907; its western boundary line is integral with the state line between Mississippi and Alabama. The population was 3,232 at the 2020 census."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/49/Red-Bay-Fourth-Ave-al.jpg/330px-Red-Bay-Fourth-Ave-al.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red_Bay%2C_Alabama"},{"title":"Rymill Bay","blocks":[{"text":"Rymill Bay is a bay, 9 nautical miles wide at its mouth and indenting 5 nautical miles between Red Rock Ridge and Bertrand Ice Piedmont along the west coast of Graham Land, Antarctica."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rymill_Bay"},{"title":"Bay","blocks":[{"text":"A bay is a recessed, coastal body of water that directly connects to a larger main body of water, such as an ocean, a lake, or another bay. A large bay is usually called a gulf, sea, sound, or bight. A cove is a small, circular bay with a narrow entrance. A fjord is an elongated bay formed by glacial action.\nThe term embayment is also used for related features, such as extinct bays or freshwater environments."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f1/Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg/330px-Aerial_photograph_of_Langness_and_the_bay_at_Castletown_13_February_2014_-_geograph.org.uk_-_3847162.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bay"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red crimson, and vary in shade from the pale red pink to the dark red burgundy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cf/Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg/330px-Delicious_fresh_strawberries_%284735910403%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Red"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG/500px-Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG/1280px-Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG/500px-Red_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"City Hall After Fire","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARed_bay_city_hall_fire.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Palmer_Land_North_USGS_Sketch.jpg/500px-Palmer_Land_North_USGS_Sketch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Palmer_Land_North_USGS_Sketch.jpg/1280px-Palmer_Land_North_USGS_Sketch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Palmer_Land_North_USGS_Sketch.jpg/500px-Palm